What attracted our attention to these two well- 
known but still insufficiently examined works of art are 
some of their very interesting iconographic features. Prior 
to their consideration, however, it seems useful to provide 
a brief overview of the cult and iconography of the holy 
fathers of Sinai and Raithou, as these hagiological and art- 
historical problems have yet to be adequately elucidated. 


